(a) When necessary for the protection of indigenous species, the department may regulate the transportation, purchase, possession, and sale of specific aquaculture products as provided for in this section.

(b) The department may determine that aquaculture products shall be accompanied by a document containing any of the following information:

(1) The name, address, and registration number of the aquaculture producer;

(2) The species;

(3) The weight, volume, or count within the container;

(4) The date of the shipment; and

(5) The name and address of the intended receiver.

(c) The department may require that certain aquaculture products be additionally identified as having been produced by aquaculture.
